  Group E -- NEW PN-PLANNER policy gap: auto-unmask too aggressive
    when the package.mask reason is profile-incompatible.
      - app-admin/mkosi-25.3
        emerge: refuses ("masked: Requires systemd"; we are on
        OpenRC).
        PN: unmasks mkosi-25.3 + sys-apps/systemd-260.1 +
        sys-apps/systemd-initctl-4 + sys-apps/gentoo-systemd-
        integration-9-r2, then fails at step 9 trying to build
        systemd on an OpenRC profile.
      Right behaviour: PN should treat package.mask comments like
      "Requires systemd" as profile-pinned (refuse to unmask under
      OpenRC), the way it already treats `make.profile` selection
      itself. Single-package impact today but the pattern is
      general (any cross-init-system mask).
      Bugzilla cross-check (`--search-bugs`): only #925191
      UNCONFIRMED (stabilise for amd64) and #971603 UNCONFIRMED
      (update to v26) -- nothing about the systemd-only mask, so
      no upstream report needed.
      NEXT: extend the auto-unmask gate to inspect the mask comment
      for known profile keywords (systemd / openrc / split-usr /
      no-multilib / merged-usr). Cheap heuristic; matches what
      `tinderbox-ng exec -- emerge -pv` reports anyway.

  Group F -- More upstream / ebuild bugs (NOT PN's problem):
      - app-admin/ryzen_smu-0.1.5 (linux-mod-r1: kernel sources
        required at /usr/src/linux). Both engines fail at setup
        phase. We don't ship kernel sources in the baseline; same
        environment limitation that already exists for clsync. Not
        worth carrying separate bug refs -- this is "build host
